From: PS3 Custom Toolchain
Subject: [PATCH] libgcc: lock-free FDE lookup on powerpc64-ps3-elf

EXPERIMENTAL CANDIDATE (not for landing): the GCC 16 thread layer made
C++ throw/catch ~1.5x slower on the PS3.  With --enable-threads=posix,
_Unwind_Find_FDE takes object_mutex on every call, and on this target
that is pthread_mutex_lock -> sys_mutex_lock: RPCS3 counts 9 lock and 9
unlock calls per throw in a two-frame unwind, none with
--enable-threads=single.

unwind-dw2-fde.c already has a lock-free lookup (a b-tree with optimistic
version locks, ATOMIC_FDE_FAST_PATH), but enables it only when
unwind-dw2-fde-dip.c includes the file.  This target has no
dl_iterate_phdr and builds the file directly, so it never got it.
t-ps3-unwind asks for it here.

What this target needs on top of the upstream machinery, all inside the
target block (ATOMIC_FDE_KEEP_TREES / ATOMIC_FDE_BOOT_RESERVE):
 - the trees hold the program's own frames, so release_registered_frames
   (a destructor) is dropped and the trees live to process end; a throw
   in a later destructor still finds its FDE, deregistration still works.
 - crtbegin registers the program from _init BEFORE the prioritized
   constructors that create the heap (83) and the syscall table (84).
   Until the runtime sets __ps3dk_heap_ready (crt1.c, at the end of 84),
   nodes come from a static reserve of 2 (one root leaf per tree: the
   PREDICTED demand of that one registration, to be measured by the
   eh-fde-registry row).  Reserve nodes are never freed.  Exhausting the
   reserve before the heap is ready traps; it never falls through to a
   malloc that cannot work yet.  The flag is a hard link-time requirement:
   with a CRT that does not define it the link fails (a custom CRT defines
   it and sets it once malloc works).
 - after that, a failed node malloc aborts instead of storing through a
   null node.
 - allocation-free counters for tests: __gcc_ps3_fde_boot_registrations,
   __gcc_ps3_fde_boot_nodes (reserve high-water), __gcc_ps3_fde_heap_nodes.
The trap and the abort are this target's contract, open for review.
Other targets are unchanged.

--- a/libgcc/config.host
+++ b/libgcc/config.host
@@ -1269,7 +1269,7 @@
 	extra_parts="$extra_parts crtbeginS.o crtendS.o crtbeginT.o ecrti.o ecrtn.o ncrti.o ncrtn.o"
 	;;
 powerpc64-ps3-elf*)
-	tmake_file="${tmake_file} rs6000/t-savresfgpr rs6000/t-ps3-crtstuff rs6000/t-ps3-gthreads"
+	tmake_file="${tmake_file} rs6000/t-savresfgpr rs6000/t-ps3-crtstuff rs6000/t-ps3-gthreads rs6000/t-ps3-unwind"
 	;;
 powerpc64-ps3-kernel-elf*)
 	tmake_file="${tmake_file} rs6000/t-savresfgpr rs6000/t-ps3-crtstuff"
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libgcc/config/rs6000/t-ps3-unwind
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
